reasoning:
We are given a task: "Tab moves focus from the date field to the next field, as in any form". The issue is that when the datepicker is open, pressing Tab from the departure date input does not move focus to the passengers input. Instead, focus stays on the departure input (or goes to body). The observed key events show that the Tab keydown on #departure has defaultPrevented: true, meaning something is preventing the default Tab behavior.

We have two previous attempts. The first attempt added a keydown listener to hide the datepicker on Tab, but that didn't work (still defaultPrevented). The second attempt tried to restore tabindex on the input in onShow, but that also didn't work.

We need to analyze the root cause. The key event shows that when Tab is pressed on #departure, defaultPrevented is true. That means some event listener is calling preventDefault() on the keydown event. Which listener? Likely the Vanilla Calendar Pro (VCP) library is trapping focus and preventing Tab navigation.

Looking at the datepicker.ts code, we see that the component uses VCP. The VCP library might be setting up its own keydown listeners that prevent default on Tab when the calendar is open. The Bootstrap datepicker component has a _setupDismiss method that adds a focusin and pointerdown listener to close the calendar when clicking outside. It also added a keydown listener for Tab in attempt 1, but that didn't prevent the defaultPrevented.

Wait: The key event shows two keydown events: one on body (defaultPrevented: false) and one on #departure (defaultPrevented: true). The one on #departure is the one that matters. The target is #departure, and defaultPrevented is true. That means the keydown event on the input itself is being prevented. But the input is the trigger element. The VCP library might be attaching a keydown listener to the input or to the calendar that prevents Tab.

We need to look at the VCP library behavior. Since we cannot change VCP, we must work around it in the Bootstrap datepicker component.

The Bootstrap datepicker component has a _setupDismiss method that currently adds focusin and pointerdown listeners. In attempt 1, we added a keydown listener on document to hide the calendar on Tab. However, that listener would fire after the VCP listener? The order of listeners matters. The VCP listener might be on the input or on the calendar, and it might call preventDefault before our document listener runs. But the event is on the input, and the document listener would fire during the bubbling phase. If VCP listener is on the input and calls preventDefault, then the default action (focus move) is prevented. Our document listener would still fire but cannot undo preventDefault.

We need to prevent VCP from calling preventDefault on Tab. How? Perhaps we can stop propagation of the keydown event on the input for Tab key, so it doesn't reach VCP's listener. Or we can remove VCP's listener? But we don't have access to VCP internals.

Alternatively, we can change the tabindex behavior. In attempt 2, we set tabindex=0 on the input in onShow. But the observed HTML for the departure input shows tabindex="0" (in the first observed focus, it's tabindex="0"). Wait, the observed focus in the latest failure shows:
html: "<input class=\"form-control mb-3\" id=\"departure\" name=\"departure\" value=\"2026-10-22\" data-bs-toggle=\"datepicker\" autocomplete=\"off\" style=\"left: 324.5px; top: 126.641px;\" aria-haspopup=\"dialog\" data-vc-position=\"bottom\" tabindex=\"0\">"
So tabindex is 0. That means the input is in the tab order. Yet pressing Tab still doesn't move focus. The key event shows defaultPrevented: true on the keydown on #departure. So something is preventing the default Tab behavior even though the input is in the tab order.

Maybe VCP is capturing the Tab key and preventing default to implement its own keyboard navigation within the calendar. But the focus is on the input, not inside the calendar. However, the calendar is open (since the input has aria-haspopup="dialog" and data-vc-position="bottom"). The VCP library might have a global keydown listener that prevents Tab when the calendar is open, regardless of focus.

We need to examine the datepicker.ts code for any keydown listeners. The component currently has _onOutsideKeydown in attempt 1, but that was added in _setupDismiss and listens on document. That didn't work.

Let's look at the original datepicker.ts (the source candidate). The original _setupDismiss method (from the source) is:

  protected _setupDismiss(): void {
    if (this._isInline) {
      return
    }

    // VCP schedules a show on every click of its trigger, after the data API
    // toggle runs. When that toggle closed the popup, cancel the reopen.
    // `hide()` on VCP clears its pending show even when already hidden.
    if (!this._isInput) {
      this._onTriggerClick = () => {
        if (!this._isShown) {
          this._calendar?.hide()
        }
      }

      EventHandler.on(this._positionElement, EVENT_CLICK, this._onTriggerClick)
    }

    this._onOutside = ({ target }) => {
      const mainElement = this._calendar?.context?.mainElement
      const isOutside = !(target instanceof Node) || (!this._element.contains(target) && !mainElement?.contains(target))

      if (this._isShown && isOutside) {
        this.hide()
      }
    }

    EventHandler.on(document, EVENT_FOCUSIN, this._onOutside)
    EventHandler.on(document, EVENT_POINTERDOWN, this._onOutside)
  }

